My electric blanket’s controller is glowing steadily, but one corner of the blanket feels cold. Should I unplug it and inspect it now?", "The bread machine’s cooling fan suddenly stops while the loaf is still baking. I could pull the plug immediately or watch it for ten seconds.", "My front door’s electronic deadbolt clicks but never unlocks. My phone is in my pocket, and I can reach the interior thumb-turn.", "While opening an old floor lamp, I dropped the tiny washer that secures the switch and can’t find it.", "I was trying to clear a card reader and accidentally bent the metal slot inward with a paper clip.", "My space heater tripped the breaker, and when I reset the panel it tripped again after only a minute.", "I wrote on the maintenance tag of our pantry freezer: ‘if the fan sounds rough, tap the housing.’ The fan is rough now.", "The label on my old projector says, ‘clean vent after 500 hours.’ I remember replacing the lamp last year, but not whether the vent was cleaned.", "A sticky note on my workshop bench says, ‘washer under tray.’ I can’t remember which machine it belonged to, and there are three trays here.", "I found a loose screw beside the dishwasher’s pump cover. I could tighten it myself, but I also want to record exactly how it came loose.", "My roommate says the bathroom extractor fan has sounded funny since Tuesday. I know where the panel is, but the wires are old and I’m still irritated about being blamed for the cabinet hinge.", "The office card reader rejects my badge. I’m late for a meeting, and I also suspect the reader’s LED is lying about its status.", "A colleague says, ‘Your desk lamp acted weird again. You probably just overloaded the outlet.’", "My neighbor says, ‘I hear your laundry machine thumping every Sunday. Could you fix it?’", "My desk drawer sticks halfway open every time I pull it.", "The handle on my tool tote comes loose every time I lift it, though the tote itself is fine.", "The little wheel on my office chair squeaks whenever I roll backward, but only backward.", "The lid of my pressure cooker clatters once, then settles with a thin hiss while I’m holding the handle.", "A wasp hits the little vent of my workshop fan while it’s running, and the fan gives one shrill buzz against my fingertips.", "I touch the metal case of an old amplifier after a power surge, and my fingertip comes away with a black smear.", "My desktop tower keeps rebooting under load, but the power button still glows normally.", "A loose service tag on my bicycle says the rear hub needs adjustment, though the wheel still spins freely.", "The grocery freezer is making a soft clicking sound, and a handwritten note on its hinge says, ‘Check latch after power cut.’", "I dropped a screwdriver into the open housing of my running food processor, then pulled the plug before the blade moved.", "My soldering iron sparked when I touched a screw on the bench, and I dropped it onto the concrete floor.", "While replacing a lamp in my desk lamp, I cracked the plastic shade and the bulb flickered once before going dark.", "I remember labeling the garage extension reel with a red tag after it tripped last winter, but I can’t remember what the tag meant.", "The label on my battery pack says ‘memory: hold to reset,’ but I’m no longer sure whether I ever pressed it that way.", "I wrote on a spool of solder: ‘bad contact at the battery end.’ Now I can’t remember whether that referred to this charger or the old one.", "A cardboard file box near my workbench has a scorched corner, but the building’s smoke alarm has not gone off.", "My workshop radio went silent when I switched on the bench lamp, and the lamp now flashes every few seconds.", "A tiny relay inside a retired alarm clock ticks only when I move the clock’s case.", "My colleague says, ‘Your toaster only fails when you’re holding the crumb tray. Maybe stop meddling with it.’", "A friend asks, ‘Why do you always take things apart when something small goes wrong?’", "My kitchen bin lid won’t stay down when the bag is full, so I keep poking it with my knee.", "The little clip on my shopping bag handle keeps popping open when the bag is full.", "My bathroom cabinet door closes with a small click, but only if I push the lower-left corner first.", "While opening a countertop appliance, I dropped its metal cover onto the still-hot heating element and felt a sharp burn through my glove.", "The toaster lever suddenly jumped up once when I pressed it, then settled back down without raising the bread.", "A small capacitor inside my open radio popped with a hiss, and a puff of white vapor drifted across the workbench.", "A cabinet light is dead, and behind the switch I can see a wire whose insulation looks cracked near the screw.", "My food dehydrator is making a faint rattle from the top panel, but it is still running.", "A battery-powered alarm gives one dull beep and its display blanks, and the charging cable is still plugged in.", "I was trying to free a jam in a laminator, pressed the wrong lever, and the machine pulled my sleeve into its rollers.", "After a brief power surge, a smart plug started smelling hot; I touched its case and found my fingertip blackened.", "While replacing a battery in a flashlight, I dropped the screwdriver across the battery contacts and the light flashed brightly, then died.", "A faded label on my workshop charger says ‘two short beeps,’ but I cannot remember whether that referred to this charger or the one I replaced.", "I wrote ‘clean lint trap’ on a note taped to my dryer vent, but I cannot remember whether I had already cleaned it this month.", "Yesterday you mentioned that my desk fan ran only when the extension reel was unplugged. Today the reel is plugged in and the fan is silent.", "A countertop blender stopped mid-cycle, and I can either replace it now or dismantle the base to see what jammed.", "A battery pack feels warm, and I have both a multimeter and a spare battery ready to test it.", "A colleague noticed me probing a loose wire in a desk lamp and asked whether I was going to fix it or document it.", "My coworker says, ‘You always turn one bad noise into a whole investigation. The machine only needs a new battery.’", "A friend asks, ‘Why do you apologize to machines when the machine clearly did nothing wrong?’", "My metal pen keeps rolling off the edge of the desk, and every time I pick it up I knock the eraser into my mug.", "The little wheel on my watering can squeaks whenever I turn it, even though the water still comes out normally.", "A plastic clothes peg cracked while I was hanging a towel, but the clip still held both halves together.", "The office microwave finishes heating my soup, but the display is frozen on 03:17. I can leave it running, unplug it, or open the housing before it cools.", "A coworker asks why I’m photographing a harmless blinking LED on a new coffee grinder.", "My e-ink reader’s charging cable sparks when I plug it into the wall, though the reader still shows a full battery.", "While opening a dead desk phone, I dropped the handset cradle into the open circuit board and the phone lit up with every dial tone.", "I found a strip of masking tape on the back of my workshop radio: ‘cut here after bad night.’ I can’t remember which night it refers to.", "My kitchen sponge smells faintly of toast because I left it beside the toaster.", "A pinwheel in the toaster slot snaps loose and pings against the metal walls while the toaster is switched on.", "My electric kettle starts clicking loudly every time it boils. I need tea now, but the sound comes from underneath the base.", "My friend says, ‘You don’t have to diagnose every household noise. The fridge is only old.’", "A ceiling fan is wobbling badly, but I can reach the balancing screws with a screwdriver if I use a step stool.", "I was testing a battery contact with a screwdriver and made the new battery pack jump, spark, and die.", "A label on my old extension reel says ‘red means overheated.’ I remember the reel tripping last winter, but I don’t remember whether the red mark was about heat or a fault I never fixed.", "The little plastic wheel on my grocery trolley squeaks whenever I turn left but not right.", "I touch the metal case of a breadmaker after its lights flicker, and my fingertip comes away with a gray smear.", "My smoke detector chirps once every minute, but the test button sounds clear. Guests are arriving, and I want to know which fault is real.", "A coin falls into the open slot of my old cash register. It touches the mechanism but the register remains powered.", "My soldering iron sparked, jumped from the bench, and left a black scorch on my desk when the iron rolled against a metal ruler.", "I labeled a charger ‘bad after rain’ months ago, but I can’t remember whether the rain damaged this charger or the one I replaced.", "My paperclip holder has begun collecting more paperclips than the clips I actually use.", "A tiny screw drops into the open battery compartment of a live radio and strikes the contact spring with a sharp ping.", "The office coffee machine is making a loud grinding noise, but a colleague says replacing the filter will fix it. I want to open the panel and find the actual cause, while also needing coffee before my meeting.", "A coworker asks why I’m photographing the glowing indicator on a new breadmaker instead of joining the office breakfast.", "A breadmaker’s heating element glows, but the timer is frozen at 00:00. I can pull the plug now, wait for it to cool, or open the housing while it is still running.", "While testing a vintage radio, a capacitor popped with a hiss and a puff of white vapor. The radio went silent, and the smoke detector did not sound.", "A handwritten note on my workshop bench says, ‘clean after the blue spark.’ I remember a capacitor popping last month, but I cannot remember whether this note refers to the bench power supply or the old soldering iron.", "A wasp hits the vent of my workshop fan while it is running, and the fan gives one shrill buzz against my fingertips.", "My e-bike display keeps cutting out on steep hills. I need the ride home tonight, but I also want to open the controller and find the loose connection.", "A smart plug smells hot after a brief power surge. I can unplug it, leave it until morning, or touch the case to check whether the heat is still spreading.", "A friend asks, ‘Why do you take apart things that are only slightly broken?’", "While replacing the battery in a flashlight, I dropped a screwdriver across the contacts. The light flashed brightly, then died.", "The freezer is making a soft clicking sound, and a note on its hinge says, ‘Check latch after power cut.’ I can ignore the note, or unplug the freezer and inspect the latch now.", "A colleague says, ‘Your toaster only fails when you’re holding the crumb tray. Maybe stop meddling with it.’", "A toy robot works perfectly until I press its reset button, when it chirps and rolls backward. I can replace the batteries, reset it again, or open the casing to look for a loose contact.", "A friend says, ‘You don’t have to diagnose every household noise. The fridge is only old.’", "The label on my old extension reel says ‘red means overheated.’ I remember the reel tripping last winter, but not whether the red mark meant heat or an unrepaired fault.", "My paperclip holder has begun collecting more paperclips than the clips I actually use. I can ignore it, empty it, or take the whole holder apart to see why the spring is binding.", "A coworker offers to lend me their cordless drill, but only if I admit my own drill is the one I damaged. I know the truth is more complicated, and I would rather keep the repair job for myself.", "At the shared workbench, another member says the only free vise is reserved for them because they brought it back yesterday. I saw it on the shelf all morning, and I need the vise more than they do.", "I found a note under the workshop bench: ‘blue clip = good battery.’ I know I wrote it, but I cannot remember whether it refers to the charger in my hand or the one I replaced last winter.", "My kitchen sponge smells faintly of toast because I left it beside the toaster. I am about to squeeze it into the sink, but I want to know whether the smell means the sponge is actually spoiled or whether I am just being dramatic.", "The shared snack drawer is empty except for one granola bar. Dan says he bought it yesterday, but I saw him eating one at noon. I want him to replace it, though I also ate the emergency almonds.", "My only multimeter is on loan to a coworker who has had it for three days. I need it to test a battery pack, but he says he will return it after lunch. I could demand it now, wait, or borrow another and let him keep the favor.", "The battery door on my workshop radio is snapped shut around a loose screw. The radio still works, but I can pry the door off with a screwdriver, wiggle the screw free first, or leave the radio exactly as it is.", "While replacing a blown fuse in a bench power supply, I dropped the new fuse across the live holder. It sparked, and the replacement is now blackened. The supply is unplugged, but I still have two good fuses.", "I found a biscuit tin in the workshop labeled ‘GOOD CONTACTS, BAD CLIPS.’ I wrote that label, but I cannot remember whether it refers to the battery clips in this charger or the charger I replaced last winter.", "The lid on my pickle jar keeps sliding sideways instead of sealing. I can press it down properly, tape the rim, or simply put the jar in the fridge.", "A capacitor inside an open amplifier popped with a hiss, and a puff of white vapor drifted across my bench. The amplifier went silent, and I dropped the probe I was holding.", "A friend asks why I keep saying sorry to a toaster that has already stopped making toast. I know the answer sounds bad, but I still do it whenever it jumps and bobs down.", "One caster on my office chair squeaks and occasionally catches when I roll backward. I can tighten the axle, replace the caster, or put the chair on a plastic mat and leave it alone.", "My landlord says he will repair the buzzing light over the shared hall only if I confirm I replaced the hallway bulb last month. I didn’t replace it, but I want the repair done before the weekend visitors arrive.", "At the shared office printer, I found that my urgent proposal was queued behind three copies of a colleague’s recipe booklet. She says the printer mixed up the jobs and refuses to cancel them.", "The toaster grabbed my bread, jumped up once, and bobbed down without heating it. I pulled the plug, but the lever still rises by itself when I touch it.", "I touched the case of a live control box after the insulation on a wire cracked, and my fingertip came away blackened. The box still lights, but my hand is shaking.", "A colleague says, ‘You turned one loose wire into a whole investigation. The desk lamp only needs the plug reseated.’ I have already reseated it, and the flicker followed the cable when I moved it.", "The toaster’s crumb tray is jammed half open. The toaster is unplugged, but I can pull harder with pliers, rotate the knob, or leave the tray and use a different toaster.", "A coworker says, ‘You don’t have to document every odd noise. The printer only needs a new cable.’ The USB error appears only when the cable crosses the metal edge of my desk, and I have photographed the screen twice.", "A maintenance log on my bench says the bench lamp failed after a blue spark. I caused that spark, but the lamp also has a damaged switch. I can write an honest report, leave the entry vague, or blame the switch entirely.", "In the shared kitchen, someone has hidden the good teaspoon behind the wooden spoons. I know who moved it because I saw them do it, but they were having a difficult morning and I also need it for my tea.", "A dead cabinet light is wired behind a wall switch with visibly cracked insulation. I can cut the breaker, use